<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia details November LSWR loading schedule.</title>
<headline>Indonesia details November LSWR loading schedule.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina has announced the loading schedule for its 3.6 million barrel low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) for lifting in November, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>November loading schedule details follow (in thousand</p>
<p>barrels):</p>
<p>LOADING FROM FLOATING STORAGE PLATINUM (OFF SUMATRA)</p>
<p>    TIMING	VOLUME	 COMPANY</p>
<p>Nov   1-3	   100	  Itochu</p>
<p>	1-3	   400	  Indoil</p>
<p>	8-10	  400	  British Petroleum (BP)</p>
<p>     16-18	  500	  Perta</p>
<p>     25-27	   60	  Perta</p>
<p>     25-27	  300	  BP</p>
<p>     25-27	   40	  Kipco</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL:   1,800</p>
<p>LOADING FROM PAKNING (SUMATRA)</p>
<p>     12-14	  200	  Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>    LOADING FROM DUMAI    (SUMATRA)</p>
<p>	5-7	   180	  Kipcou</p>
<p>	5-7	    20	  Indoil</p>
<p>     15-17	  200	  Indoil</p>
<p>     25-27	  200	  BP</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL:    600</p>
<p>LOADING FROM SAMBU JETTY</p>
<p>     23-25	   200	 BP</p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     200</p>
<p>LOADING FROM BALIKPAPAN (KALIMANTAN, BORNEO)</p>
<p>     10-12	   200	 FEI</p>
<p>     14-16	   200	 FEI</p>
<p>     21-23	   140	 FEI</p>
<p>     21-23	    60	 Itochu</p>
<p>     25-27	    20	 BP</p>
<p>     25-27	   180	 Indoil</p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     800</p>
<p>    TOTAL	  3,600</p>
<p>-- Kiyoshi Takanaka in Tokyo (+81-3-5473-3706)</p>
<p>-- Ang Bee Lin in Singapore (+65-870-3082)</p>
